Clean-Room Engineering & License Boundary Policy
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

PiPiBot is released under the MIT License. All source code, prompts, UI
components, and visual assets in this repository are original, clean-room
implementations unless explicitly noted below.

When PiPiBot absorbs architectural concepts or UX patterns from upstream
open-source projects whose licenses carry additional conditions (such as
modified Apache-2.0 licenses), we follow strict clean-room rules:

  1. ZERO source code, prompt templates, frontend components, logos, or
     binary assets are copied verbatim from non-MIT repositories.
  2. Every inspired module is designed and implemented independently from
     scratch in Swift 6 / TypeScript for PiPiBot's native local-first stack.
  3. Upstream projects are credited transparently here, in README files,
     in roadmap documents, and in source file headers.

